From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] server: files report Everyone as read and run only, as Wine on Linux does

The console's file system reports every file as 0777 and ignores chmod, so every DACL read "Everyone: modify" and a DACL that was set never showed.
Blizzard's Agent checks a folder's DACL against what it wants (Everyone read and run only, 0x1200a9), found 0x1301ff, rewrote the ACL of each of 10,500 files at every
start (the SetNamedSecurityInfoW trace of 2026-10-12) and marked the game unplayable: Permissions check failure (2123), the game shows Update.
Wine on Linux under umask 022 reports exactly 0x1200a9 (the host oracle, tests/agent-permissions-probe.c). Group and others now lose write in the
descriptor made from the mode; the owner keeps everything, and the kernel decides access as before.
---
diff --git a/server/file.c b/server/file.c
--- a/server/file.c
+++ b/server/file.c
@@ -546,9 +546,19 @@
         return obj->sd;
 
     sd = get_xattr_sd( unix_fd );
-    if (!sd) sd = mode_to_sd( st.st_mode,
-                              security_unix_uid_to_sid( st.st_uid ),
-                              token_get_primary_group( current->process->token ));
+    if (!sd)
+    {
+        mode_t shown = st.st_mode;
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+        /* The console's file system reports every file as 0777 and ignores chmod, so every DACL read "Everyone: modify" and no
+         * change ever showed. Wine on Linux, under the usual umask 022, reports Everyone as read and run only; so does this, and a
+         * program that checks a folder's permissions gets the Linux answer. Blizzard's Agent wants exactly that: finding more, it
+         * set the ACL of each of 10,500 files at every start and marked the game unplayable (error 2123, the game: Update). */
+        shown &= ~(S_IWGRP | S_IWOTH);
+#endif
+        sd = mode_to_sd( shown, security_unix_uid_to_sid( st.st_uid ),
+                         token_get_primary_group( current->process->token ));
+    }
     if (!sd) return obj->sd;
 
     *mode = st.st_mode;
